## 1. Objective
Currently, the visible SVG Piano Roll in `src/components/WebGPUCanvas.tsx` only attaches an `onClick` handler to note `<g>` elements, while the PIXI background canvas has `pointerEvents = 'none'`. As a result, clicking and dragging a note on the Piano Roll does not move the note or update the `.ten` code. Furthermore, `SplitWorkspace.handleCanvasMutation` only calls `resizeDuration` (ignoring vertical pitch changes), and `TopologicalMutator.ts` lacks support for transposing a single dragged voice inside a chord bracket (`[c4 e4 g4]:2`) or resizing sticky-duration tokens (`d` in `c4:8 d e`).

This contract implements full bi-directional click-and-drag editing on the Piano Roll:
1. **Vertical Drag (Pitch Transposition):** Clicking and dragging any note body up or down on the Piano Roll shows a live optimistic preview of the new pitch row and pitch name (`e.g. E4 (+4st)`) and rewrites the token's pitch in `.ten` source code on mouse release—including single notes, sticky-octave notes, and individual voices inside `[...]` chords.
2. **Horizontal / Right-Edge Drag (Quantized Duration Resizing):** Dragging a note's right-edge resize handle (`note-resize-handle-<idx>`) or dragging horizontally snaps the width delta to `1/16`th-note grid steps and rewrites the rational duration in `.ten` source code on mouse release.
3. **Full Undo/Redo Integration:** Every drag mutation commits through `CommandManager` so `Cmd/Ctrl + Z` and `Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + Z` undo and redo Piano Roll drags in a single step.

